in terms of the extra blurring delay when the 'add to my list' bar appears, i'm not sure how to fix it. i asked gemini, but did not get a super clear answer on how to fix it other than this:
# The perceived delay or lag happens because of how browsers handle backdrop-filter during opacity transitions.

# When the parent overlay fades in from opacity: 0 to opacity: 1, the browser's graphics engine is forced to recalculate and re-render the background blur frame-by-frame at fractional opacities. On many GPUs, this creates a slight rendering lag where the blur takes a moment to "settle." 
